# SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
# Lumen OS on the XGIMI Play 6: Wi-Fi of the newer batches with the AICSemi AIC8800D80X2 USB chip (368b:8d90).
# XGIMI's V1.7.116 vendor has only MediaTek drivers (its wlan_dongle_detect and dongle.cfg know 0e8d only), so on
# those units Wi-Fi is dead. play6_aic.sh looks at the USB chip first and loads our AIC modules
# (tools/play6/aic, /system/etc/aic8800) only when it is 368b:8d90 or 368b:8d91; a MediaTek unit gets nothing.
# Vendor untouched: the stock firmware_class / cfg80211 modules, wpa_supplicant and Wi-Fi HAL drive wlan0 as
# they do for MediaTek (device test 2026-10-28). Started only once the boot has completed, as in the manual test
# that worked (the first pre-release loaded it at post-fs-data and that unit did not finish its boot; until that
# is understood nothing of ours runs before boot_completed); play6_aic.sh then restarts Wi-Fi and the Bluetooth
# HAL so they pick the chip up. Started, not exec'd: init never waits for it.
on property:sys.boot_completed=1
    start play6_aic

service play6_aic /system/bin/sh /system/etc/xgimi/play6_aic.sh
    user root
    group root
    seclabel u:r:su:s0
    oneshot
    disabled
